  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To find the additive inverse of the number $24$, we change its sign by placing a minus symbol $(-)$ in front of it. So, we obtain \n\n$$\n-\\,(24)=-24.\n$$\n\nTo check our work, we simply add the inverse to the original number. If we're correct, we should get zero.\n\n$$\n24+(-24)=24-24=0\\,✓\n$$",
